      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>Behold God is my salvation, etc.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>The esteemed community living&nbsp; in Fustat&nbsp;</li>\n<li>-4. may their Rock bless them, a(men) n(esah) s(elah), are&nbsp; hereby informed that the community has received a letter from our lord&nbsp; the Nagid, l(ong) m(ay he live),&nbsp;</li>\n<li></li>\n<li>greeting you and praying for you and your children,&nbsp;</li>\n<li>men, women, children and young men, and ordering&nbsp; you with utmost</li>\n<li>command to be of one heart, to love one&nbsp;</li>\n<li>-9.&nbsp; another, to strive hard to perform the religious commandments, which&nbsp; as is well known from your charitableness you are accustomed to doing.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li></li>\n<li>No one shall transgress the authority of the religious law or&nbsp;</li>\n<li>go&nbsp; to the gentiles' (courts). Whoever transgresses and goes&nbsp;</li>\n<li>to the gentile courts prior to appearing before the Jewish court for \"informers\"&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>in Cairo and receiving their permission is under a&nbsp;</li>\n<li>curse and subject to a warning, and again, a warning against disobedience.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>May God the exal(ted) be your succor and make your habitations&nbsp; prosper,&nbsp;</li>\n<li>and may you not exclude us from your thoughts. And peace.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>[postscript]: Read them in the l(arge) synagogue of the&nbsp; J(erusalemites) on Thursday,&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Friday, and on the Sabbath, and send them to us on&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Sunday. And peace.</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
